 "text": "A rocket scientist invented this toy by accident in his bathroom. In 1982, Lonnie Johnson, an engineer who worked on NASA missions, is building a cooling system that runs on water. He tests a homemade nozzle on his bathroom sink. Whoosh! A blast of water shoots across the room. This would make an amazing water gun. He builds a prototype, but it takes years to get a toy company on board. He keeps pushing. Finally, a company called Laramie says yes. In 1990, it hits stores as the Power Drencher. Then it gets a new name, the Super Soaker. In three years, Laramie sells about 27 million of them. A science experiment that soaked a whole generation. Every legend has a beginning.",
